[2026-02-04T00:03:08.667Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011pGKb2WkXJRTxmZkwT4m3x","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"climate change claims debate 2026\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"5 climate court battles to watch in 2026 - E&E News by POLITICO\",\"url\":\"https://www.eenews.net/articles/5-climate-court-battles-to-watch-in-2026/\"},{\"title\":\"What to Watch in Climate Litigation in 2026 - Union of Concerned Scientists\",\"url\":\"https://blog.ucs.org/delta-merner/what-to-watch-in-climate-litigation-in-2026/\"},{\"title\":\"Climate Litigation Updates (January 7, 2026) | Sabin Center for Climate Change Law\",\"url\":\"https://climate.law.columbia.edu/news/climate-litigation-updates-january-7-2026\"},{\"title\":\"2026 will be a turning point for climate litigation Materia Rinnovabile | Renewable Matter\",\"url\":\"https://www.renewablematter.eu/en/2026-will-be-a-turning-point-for-climate-litigation\"},{\"title\":\"Ten climate litigation moments to look out for in 2026\",\"url\":\"https://www.the-wave.net/climate-litigation-preview-january-2026/\"},{\"title\":\"Climate Litigation News and Case Updates | January 26–30, 2026\",\"url\":\"https://www.climate-court.com/post/climate-litigation-news-and-case-updates-january-26-30-2026\"},{\"title\":\"Climate Change | Pros, Cons, Debate, Arguments, Global Warming, & Environmental Activism | Britannica\",\"url\":\"https://www.britannica.com/procon/climate-change-debate\"},{\"title\":\"E&E News: 5 climate court battles to watch in 2026\",\"url\":\"https://subscriber.politicopro.com/article/eenews/2026/01/06/5-climate-court-battles-to-watch-in-2026-00700888\"},{\"title\":\"Climate Litigation Updates (January 30, 2026) | Sabin Center for Climate Change Law\",\"url\":\"https://climate.law.columbia.edu/news/climate-litigation-updates-january-30-2026\"},{\"title\":\"Understanding climate change in America: Skepticism, dogmatism and personal experience | News, Sports, Jobs - The Express\",\"url\":\"https://www.lockhaven.com/opinion/columns/2026/01/understanding-climate-change-in-america-skepticism-dogmatism-and-personal-experience/\"}]\n\nHere are the results for the search \"climate change claims debate 2026\":\n\n## Climate Change Claims and Debate in 2026\n\nThe search results show that 2026 is shaping up to be a pivotal year for climate-related legal battles and debates, with multiple court cases and litigation developments worldwide.\n\n### Key Climate Court Battles\n\nClimate could become a major issue at the U.S. Supreme Court in 2026, as the justices consider an oil industry bid to stop states, cities and counties nationwide from holding the fossil fuel industry financially accountable for rising global temperatures.\n\nTwo of the DOJ lawsuits — against New York and Vermont — aim to invalidate state laws creating \"climate Superfunds\" that seek payment from energy producers for greenhouse gas emissions.\n\n### International Developments\n\nIn 2026, courts are becoming the new battleground for the climate crisis. Ukraine is preparing to file the first claim for climate reparations in history against Russia, estimating the cost of the 236.8 million tonnes of CO₂ equivalent generated by the invasion at $43 billion.\n\nOn January 28, 2026, a Dutch Court found human rights violations in climate adaptation and mitigation in the Bonaire climate case (Stichting Greenpeace Nederland v. The State of the Netherlands).\n\n### Litigation Trends\n\nIn 2026, the most important development to watch is whether climate accountability cases finally move into substantive discovery, evidentiary hearings, and trial.\n\nGlobally, roughly a quarter of newly filed climate-related cases now involve arguments that are not aligned with climate goals, many of them in the United States. These include challenges to ESG, disclosure requirements, renewable energy development, and state-level accountability laws.\n\n### Youth Climate Cases\n\nLa Rose v His Majesty the King starts on October 26, 2026 in Vancouver, British Columbia. Fifteen Canadian young people from seven provinces and one territory claim Canada's ongoing contribution to climate change violates their rights to life, liberty and security of the person under the Canadian Charter of Rights and Freedoms.\n\n### The Science Debate\n\nScientists are trained to be professional skeptics: to always judge the validity of a claim or finding on the basis of objective, empirical evidence. They are not cynics; they just ask themselves and each other a lot of questions.\n\nThe pro side of the climate debate argues that overwhelming scientific consensus finds human activity primarily responsible for climate change, and that rising levels of human-produced gases released into the atmosphere create a greenhouse effect that traps heat and causes global warming.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fc19be83-c5d4-4d22-a1ea-f9f460ee03af","uuid":"f61b06c9-4d28-4286-9ae5-182b112a30f6","tool_use_result":{"query":"climate change claims debate 2026","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01VygCwAN59zvkLtQrL3zmrv","content":[{"title":"5 climate court battles to watch in 2026 - E&E News by POLITICO","url":"https://www.eenews.net/articles/5-climate-court-battles-to-watch-in-2026/"},{"title":"What to Watch in Climate Litigation in 2026 - Union of Concerned Scientists","url":"https://blog.ucs.org/delta-merner/what-to-watch-in-climate-litigation-in-2026/"},{"title":"Climate Litigation Updates (January 7, 2026) | Sabin Center for Climate Change Law","url":"https://climate.law.columbia.edu/news/climate-litigation-updates-january-7-2026"},{"title":"2026 will be a turning point for climate litigation Materia Rinnovabile | Renewable Matter","url":"https://www.renewablematter.eu/en/2026-will-be-a-turning-point-for-climate-litigation"},{"title":"Ten climate litigation moments to look out for in 2026","url":"https://www.the-wave.net/climate-litigation-preview-january-2026/"},{"title":"Climate Litigation News and Case Updates | January 26–30, 2026","url":"https://www.climate-court.com/post/climate-litigation-news-and-case-updates-january-26-30-2026"},{"title":"Climate Change | Pros, Cons, Debate, Arguments, Global Warming, & Environmental Activism | Britannica","url":"https://www.britannica.com/procon/climate-change-debate"},{"title":"E&E News: 5 climate court battles to watch in 2026","url":"https://subscriber.politicopro.com/article/eenews/2026/01/06/5-climate-court-battles-to-watch-in-2026-00700888"},{"title":"Climate Litigation Updates (January 30, 2026) | Sabin Center for Climate Change Law","url":"https://climate.law.columbia.edu/news/climate-litigation-updates-january-30-2026"},{"title":"Understanding climate change in America: Skepticism, dogmatism and personal experience | News, Sports, Jobs - The Express","url":"https://www.lockhaven.com/opinion/columns/2026/01/understanding-climate-change-in-america-skepticism-dogmatism-and-personal-experience/"}]},"Here are the results for the search \"climate change claims debate 2026\":\n\n## Climate Change Claims and Debate in 2026\n\nThe search results show that 2026 is shaping up to be a pivotal year for climate-related legal battles and debates, with multiple court cases and litigation developments worldwide.\n\n### Key Climate Court Battles\n\nClimate could become a major issue at the U.S. Supreme Court in 2026, as the justices consider an oil industry bid to stop states, cities and counties nationwide from holding the fossil fuel industry financially accountable for rising global temperatures.\n\nTwo of the DOJ lawsuits — against New York and Vermont — aim to invalidate state laws creating \"climate Superfunds\" that seek payment from energy producers for greenhouse gas emissions.\n\n### International Developments\n\nIn 2026, courts are becoming the new battleground for the climate crisis. Ukraine is preparing to file the first claim for climate reparations in history against Russia, estimating the cost of the 236.8 million tonnes of CO₂ equivalent generated by the invasion at $43 billion.\n\nOn January 28, 2026, a Dutch Court found human rights violations in climate adaptation and mitigation in the Bonaire climate case (Stichting Greenpeace Nederland v. The State of the Netherlands).\n\n### Litigation Trends\n\nIn 2026, the most important development to watch is whether climate accountability cases finally move into substantive discovery, evidentiary hearings, and trial.\n\nGlobally, roughly a quarter of newly filed climate-related cases now involve arguments that are not aligned with climate goals, many of them in the United States. These include challenges to ESG, disclosure requirements, renewable energy development, and state-level accountability laws.\n\n### Youth Climate Cases\n\nLa Rose v His Majesty the King starts on October 26, 2026 in Vancouver, British Columbia. Fifteen Canadian young people from seven provinces and one territory claim Canada's ongoing contribution to climate change violates their rights to life, liberty and security of the person under the Canadian Charter of Rights and Freedoms.\n\n### The Science Debate\n\nScientists are trained to be professional skeptics: to always judge the validity of a claim or finding on the basis of objective, empirical evidence. They are not cynics; they just ask themselves and each other a lot of questions.\n\nThe pro side of the climate debate argues that overwhelming scientific consensus finds human activity primarily responsible for climate change, and that rising levels of human-produced gases released into the atmosphere create a greenhouse effect that traps heat and causes global warming."],"durationSeconds":19.426739200000004}}
[2026-02-04T00:03:08.964Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FapGA6sjMX1vMZWiZeHs6x","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"AI technology claims controversy 2026\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"AI-Related Claims and Other Securities Litigation Trends to Watch | Skadden, Arps, Slate, Meagher & Flom LLP\",\"url\":\"https://www.skadden.com/insights/publications/2026/2026-insights/litigation-controversy/ai-related-claims-and-other-securities-litigation-trends-to-watch\"},{\"title\":\"AI update for 2026 | Horizon Scanning\",\"url\":\"https://www.slaughterandmay.com/horizon-scanning/2026/digital/ai-update-for-2026/\"},{\"title\":\"What we’ve been getting wrong about AI’s truth crisis | MIT Technology Review\",\"url\":\"https://www.technologyreview.com/2026/02/02/1132068/what-weve-been-getting-wrong-about-ais-truth-crisis/\"},{\"title\":\"AI Infringement Case Updates: November 24, 2025: McKool Smith\",\"url\":\"https://www.mckoolsmith.com/newsroom-ailitigation-46\"},{\"title\":\"Generative AI Lawsuits Timeline: Legal Cases vs. OpenAI, Microsoft, Anthropic, Google, Nvidia, Perplexity, Salesforce, Apple and More - Sustainable Tech Partner for IT Service Providers\",\"url\":\"https://sustainabletechpartner.com/topics/ai/generative-ai-lawsuit-timeline/\"},{\"title\":\"Top 50 AI Scandals [2026] - DigitalDefynd Education\",\"url\":\"https://digitaldefynd.com/IQ/top-ai-scandals/\"},{\"title\":\"AI Litigation Tracker | McKool Smith: McKool Smith\",\"url\":\"https://www.mckoolsmith.com/newsroom-ailitigation\"},{\"title\":\"26 Biggest AI Controversies of 2025-2026 | The Latest Edition\",\"url\":\"https://www.crescendo.ai/blog/ai-controversies\"},{\"title\":\"85 Predictions for AI and the Law in 2026\",\"url\":\"https://natlawreview.com/article/85-predictions-ai-and-law-2026\"},{\"title\":\"Whistleblower says Israeli military contractor used Google's Gemini AI - The Washington Post\",\"url\":\"https://www.washingtonpost.com/technology/2026/02/01/google-ai-israel-military/\"}]\n\nHere are the search results for \"AI technology claims controversy 2026\":\n\n## AI Technology Claims Controversies in 2026\n\nThe search results reveal several significant AI-related controversies and legal developments in 2026:\n\n### Securities Litigation & \"AI-Washing\" Claims\nCurrent securities litigation trends are likely to continue through 2026, with plaintiffs increasingly bringing suits over AI claims and private lending. AI-related class actions have outpaced other categories and are set to shape the litigation landscape, with plaintiffs filing complaints based on allegations of \"AI-washing\" — misrepresentations about AI capabilities or revenues. These include claims about:\n- Overstated AI-driven efficiencies, misleadingly rebranded legacy technology as AI, concealed licensing or performance issues, and exaggerated the pace and feasibility of AI integration.\n\n### Regulatory Focus on AI Misrepresentation\nRegulators are keeping a keen eye on \"AI washing\" - the practice of making false or exaggerated claims about the use of AI, with the US Federal Trade Commission having underscored its focus on \"ensuring the promise of new technology isn't misused as a means to mislead consumers.\"\n\n### AI and the \"Truth Crisis\"\nConcerns are growing about an era of \"truth decay\" where AI content dupes us, shapes our beliefs even when we catch the lie, and erodes societal trust in the process. The US Department of Homeland Security is now using AI video generators from Google and Adobe to make content shared with the public, as immigration agencies have flooded social media with content to support mass deportation efforts.\n\n### Major Copyright Lawsuits\nLawsuits against AI giants OpenAI, Anthropic, and Perplexity are set to continue headlining intellectual property developments in California federal courts in 2026. Writers including Pulitzer Prize-winning journalist John Carreyrou filed a copyright lawsuit accusing six AI giants of using pirated copies of their books to train large language models, claiming Anthropic, Google, OpenAI, Meta Platforms, xAI and Perplexity committed a \"deliberate act of theft.\"\n\n### Google-Israel Military AI Controversy\nA whistleblower complaint filed with the SEC claims that Google breached its own ethics rules to help an Israeli contractor apply AI to drone surveillance video.\n\n### AI Chatbot Controversies\nIn early 2026, Elon Musk's AI chatbot Grok became the center of a global firestorm following an update to its image-generation model, Aurora, which allowed users to manipulate photographs of real people.\n\nThese controversies highlight ongoing concerns about AI ethics, intellectual property rights, government transparency, and the potential for AI to be used for misleading claims or harmful purposes.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fc19be83-c5d4-4d22-a1ea-f9f460ee03af","uuid":"65e3a4e0-0754-42dc-9a0d-ef4721958f58","tool_use_result":{"query":"AI technology claims controversy 2026","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_013dgWdyBfrcVVatTBpr9HPr","content":[{"title":"AI-Related Claims and Other Securities Litigation Trends to Watch | Skadden, Arps, Slate, Meagher & Flom LLP","url":"https://www.skadden.com/insights/publications/2026/2026-insights/litigation-controversy/ai-related-claims-and-other-securities-litigation-trends-to-watch"},{"title":"AI update for 2026 | Horizon Scanning","url":"https://www.slaughterandmay.com/horizon-scanning/2026/digital/ai-update-for-2026/"},{"title":"What we’ve been getting wrong about AI’s truth crisis | MIT Technology Review","url":"https://www.technologyreview.com/2026/02/02/1132068/what-weve-been-getting-wrong-about-ais-truth-crisis/"},{"title":"AI Infringement Case Updates: November 24, 2025: McKool Smith","url":"https://www.mckoolsmith.com/newsroom-ailitigation-46