[2026-02-04T00:03:36.302Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Mo196gQr8Xf753JuCScYTs","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"cryptocurrency bitcoin regulation 2026\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"US Crypto Policy Tracker Regulatory Developments\",\"url\":\"https://www.lw.com/en/us-crypto-policy-tracker/regulatory-developments\"},{\"title\":\"Crypto in 2026: The Democratization of Digital Assets | HUB | K&L Gates\",\"url\":\"https://www.klgates.com/Crypto-in-2026-The-Democratization-of-Digital-Assets-1-29-2026\"},{\"title\":\"US Crypto Regulation Update 2026: Bitcoin Holds Amid Senate Delays\",\"url\":\"https://www.equiti.com/sc-en/news/crypto-hub/us-regulatory-setback-and-market-reaction/\"},{\"title\":\"Blockchain & Cryptocurrency Laws and Regulations 2026 | Cleary Gottlieb\",\"url\":\"https://www.clearygottlieb.com/news-and-insights/publication-listing/blockchain-cryptocurrency-laws-and-regulations-26\"},{\"title\":\"Blockchain and Cryptocurrency Laws and Regulations 2026\",\"url\":\"https://www.globallegalinsights.com/practice-areas/blockchain-cryptocurrency-laws-and-regulations/\"},{\"title\":\"IRS Rule Changes In 2026 Bitcoin, Ethereum, XRP Traders Need To Know About\",\"url\":\"https://finance.yahoo.com/news/irs-rule-changes-2026-bitcoin-033050163.html\"},{\"title\":\"Crypto’s Rules Are Here. 2026 Will Be About Making Them Work\",\"url\":\"https://news.bloomberglaw.com/legal-exchange-insights-and-commentary/cryptos-rules-are-here-2026-will-be-about-making-them-work\"},{\"title\":\"US Crypto Regulation in 2026: Key Laws, SEC Changes, and What Comes Next\",\"url\":\"https://coinpedia.org/news/us-crypto-regulation-in-2026-key-laws-sec-changes-and-what-comes-next/\"},{\"title\":\"Top US Crypto Bills To Watch in 2026: Market Structure, Stablecoins & More\",\"url\":\"https://finance.yahoo.com/news/top-us-crypto-bills-watch-100215687.html\"},{\"title\":\"PwC: 2026 will be the year crypto rules move from drafts to reality\",\"url\":\"https://www.coindesk.com/policy/2026/01/22/crypto-regulation-to-become-global-reality-this-year-pwc-says\"}]\n\nHere's what I found about cryptocurrency and Bitcoin regulation in 2026:\n\n## Key Regulatory Developments\n\n### Major U.S. Legislation\n\nThe GENIUS Act, signed into law on July 18, 2025, established the first comprehensive federal cryptocurrency framework in U.S. history. This bipartisan legislation, which passed 68–30 in the Senate and 308–122 in the House, created a regulatory structure for the $260 billion stablecoin market, mandating 100% reserve backing and establishing federal and state licensing pathways.\n\nFull implementation of the GENIUS Act is targeted for 2026, with regulators required to finalize rules by July 18, 2026.\n\nThe U.S. House of Representatives passed the Digital Asset Market Clarity Act of 2025 (the \"CLARITY Act\") on July 17, 2025. The U.S. Senate is considering this bill. If enacted, the CLARITY Act would create a comprehensive new regulatory regime for \"digital commodities,\" including BTC, ETH, and other common cryptocurrencies.\n\n### Regulatory Outlook for 2026\n\nPwC said 2026 is the year regulations move from drawing boards to reality. Crypto regulation will shift from debate to execution and competition among jurisdictions to attract capital and legitimacy.\n\nCompanies and practitioners should expect 2026 to be less about crafting new regulations and more about refining, connecting, and operationalizing the ones in place.\n\n### Tax Changes\n\nBeginning in 2026, centralized exchanges will be required to follow the same cost-basis reporting rules as traditional brokerages. This means platforms must report both purchase and sale cost basis details for every U.S. customer's digital asset transaction.\n\nCost basis reporting becomes mandatory under rules created by the 2021 Infrastructure Bill, aimed at tightening crypto tax compliance.\n\n### Market Status and Outlook\n\nCryptocurrency markets have shown mixed performance in the wake of regulatory uncertainty. Bitcoin has traded in a narrow range near $95,000–$96,000, reflecting a degree of resilience despite regulatory headwinds.\n\nFollowing the Senate's postponement of the crypto market structure bill, regulatory clarity in the U.S. is now likely to unfold gradually through 2026. Committees are expected to revisit markups, but broader political dynamics, including the 2026 midterms, may push final legislation into late 2026 or beyond.\n\n### Global Developments\n\nThe EU's Markets in Crypto-Assets Regulation (MiCA) achieved full implementation, creating the world's most comprehensive crypto framework. The UK took a measured approach, developing regulations for late 2026 implementation.\n\nCalifornia's Digital Financial Assets Law comes into force on July 1, requiring crypto companies serving state residents to obtain licenses. At the same time, states such as Texas are advancing Bitcoin reserve plans, pointing to growing government involvement in digital assets.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fc19be83-c5d4-4d22-a1ea-f9f460ee03af","uuid":"9a070cc5-8720-4c9e-8d87-e35f059a650f","tool_use_result":{"query":"cryptocurrency bitcoin regulation 2026","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_018f82oeCZAe2a6GesUTENJe","content":[{"title":"US Crypto Policy Tracker Regulatory Developments","url":"https://www.lw.com/en/us-crypto-policy-tracker/regulatory-developments"},{"title":"Crypto in 2026: The Democratization of Digital Assets | HUB | K&L Gates","url":"https://www.klgates.com/Crypto-in-2026-The-Democratization-of-Digital-Assets-1-29-2026"},{"title":"US Crypto Regulation Update 2026: Bitcoin Holds Amid Senate Delays","url":"https://www.equiti.com/sc-en/news/crypto-hub/us-regulatory-setback-and-market-reaction/"},{"title":"Blockchain & Cryptocurrency Laws and Regulations 2026 | Cleary Gottlieb","url":"https://www.clearygottlieb.com/news-and-insights/publication-listing/blockchain-cryptocurrency-laws-and-regulations-26"},{"title":"Blockchain and Cryptocurrency Laws and Regulations 2026","url":"https://www.globallegalinsights.com/practice-areas/blockchain-cryptocurrency-laws-and-regulations/"},{"title":"IRS Rule Changes In 2026 Bitcoin, Ethereum, XRP Traders Need To Know About","url":"https://finance.yahoo.com/news/irs-rule-changes-2026-bitcoin-033050163.html"},{"title":"Crypto’s Rules Are Here. 2026 Will Be About Making Them Work","url":"https://news.bloomberglaw.com/legal-exchange-insights-and-commentary/cryptos-rules-are-here-2026-will-be-about-making-them-work"},{"title":"US Crypto Regulation in 2026: Key Laws, SEC Changes, and What Comes Next","url":"https://coinpedia.org/news/us-crypto-regulation-in-2026-key-laws-sec-changes-and-what-comes-next/"},{"title":"Top US Crypto Bills To Watch in 2026: Market Structure, Stablecoins & More","url":"https://finance.yahoo.com/news/top-us-crypto-bills-watch-100215687.html"},{"title":"PwC: 2026 will be the year crypto rules move from drafts to reality","url":"https://www.coindesk.com/policy/2026/01/22/crypto-regulation-to-become-global-reality-this-year-pwc-says"}]},"Here's what I found about cryptocurrency and Bitcoin regulation in 2026:\n\n## Key Regulatory Developments\n\n### Major U.S. Legislation\n\nThe GENIUS Act, signed into law on July 18, 2025, established the first comprehensive federal cryptocurrency framework in U.S. history. This bipartisan legislation, which passed 68–30 in the Senate and 308–122 in the House, created a regulatory structure for the $260 billion stablecoin market, mandating 100% reserve backing and establishing federal and state licensing pathways.\n\nFull implementation of the GENIUS Act is targeted for 2026, with regulators required to finalize rules by July 18, 2026.\n\nThe U.S. House of Representatives passed the Digital Asset Market Clarity Act of 2025 (the \"CLARITY Act\") on July 17, 2025. The U.S. Senate is considering this bill. If enacted, the CLARITY Act would create a comprehensive new regulatory regime for \"digital commodities,\" including BTC, ETH, and other common cryptocurrencies.\n\n### Regulatory Outlook for 2026\n\nPwC said 2026 is the year regulations move from drawing boards to reality. Crypto regulation will shift from debate to execution and competition among jurisdictions to attract capital and legitimacy.\n\nCompanies and practitioners should expect 2026 to be less about crafting new regulations and more about refining, connecting, and operationalizing the ones in place.\n\n### Tax Changes\n\nBeginning in 2026, centralized exchanges will be required to follow the same cost-basis reporting rules as traditional brokerages. This means platforms must report both purchase and sale cost basis details for every U.S. customer's digital asset transaction.\n\nCost basis reporting becomes mandatory under rules created by the 2021 Infrastructure Bill, aimed at tightening crypto tax compliance.\n\n### Market Status and Outlook\n\nCryptocurrency markets have shown mixed performance in the wake of regulatory uncertainty. Bitcoin has traded in a narrow range near $95,000–$96,000, reflecting a degree of resilience despite regulatory headwinds.\n\nFollowing the Senate's postponement of the crypto market structure bill, regulatory clarity in the U.S. is now likely to unfold gradually through 2026. Committees are expected to revisit markups, but broader political dynamics, including the 2026 midterms, may push final legislation into late 2026 or beyond.\n\n### Global Developments\n\nThe EU's Markets in Crypto-Assets Regulation (MiCA) achieved full implementation, creating the world's most comprehensive crypto framework. The UK took a measured approach, developing regulations for late 2026 implementation.\n\nCalifornia's Digital Financial Assets Law comes into force on July 1, requiring crypto companies serving state residents to obtain licenses. At the same time, states such as Texas are advancing Bitcoin reserve plans, pointing to growing government involvement in digital assets."],"durationSeconds":19.3198059}}
[2026-02-04T00:03:37.423Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JzR33UgZxyKRAMuNd46CFK","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"social media misinformation fact check 2026\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"COLUMN: How do you know if what you see on social media is real? - Marblehead Current\",\"url\":\"https://marbleheadcurrent.org/2026/01/27/column-how-do-you-know-if-what-you-see-on-social-media-is-real/\"},{\"title\":\"Combating Misinformation by Sharing the Truth: a Study on the Spread of Fact-Checks on Social Media - PMC\",\"url\":\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9188446/\"},{\"title\":\"You've been fact-checked! Examining the effectiveness of social media fact-checking against the spread of misinformation - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S2772503023000506\"},{\"title\":\"Tools That Fight Disinformation Online | RAND\",\"url\":\"https://www.rand.org/research/projects/truth-decay/fighting-disinformation/search.html\"},{\"title\":\"The most effective online fact-checkers? Your peers\",\"url\":\"https://www.rochester.edu/newscenter/crowdsourcing-fact-checking-community-notes-social-media-676142/\"},{\"title\":\"Social Media Fact-Checking: The Effects of News Literacy and News Trust on the Intent to Verify Health-Related Information - PMC\",\"url\":\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10606871/\"},{\"title\":\"Debunking Viral Claims Archives - FactCheck.org\",\"url\":\"https://www.factcheck.org/fake-news/\"},{\"title\":\"Debunking “fake news” on social media: Immediate and short-term effects of fact-checking and media literacy interventions - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S004727272500043X\"},{\"title\":\"Flagging misinformation on social media reduces engagement, study finds | Yale News\",\"url\":\"https://news.yale.edu/2025/09/25/flagging-misinformation-social-media-reduces-engagement-study-finds\"},{\"title\":\"Warning labels from fact checkers work — even if you don’t trust them | MIT Sloan\",\"url\":\"https://mitsloan.mit.edu/press/warning-labels-fact-checkers-work-even-if-you-dont-trust-them\"}]\n\nHere are the search results for \"social media misinformation fact check 2026\":\n\n## Key Findings\n\n### Current State of Misinformation\nSocial media is filled with more false information than ever before. In recent months, experts have noticed a big rise in misinformation and disinformation online. Misinformation means sharing something wrong by mistake, while disinformation is a lie spread on purpose. Both are spreading quickly on platforms like Facebook, Instagram, X (formerly Twitter) and TikTok.\n\n### Recent Developments in Fact-Checking\n\nMeta (which owns Facebook and Instagram) recently decided to end its program of using outside fact-checkers on its platforms. Many people are worried that without those fact-checks, it might become even easier for fake posts to spread unchecked.\n\nFrom late 2016 to early 2025, FactCheck.org was one of several organizations working with Meta to debunk misinformation shared on Meta's social media platforms.\n\n### Community Notes and Crowdsourced Fact-Checking\n\nPointing out potentially misleading posts on social media significantly reduces the number of reposts, likes, replies, and views generated by such content. This suggests that crowd-sourced fact-checking can be a useful tool for curbing online misinformation.\n\nEarlier this year, the social media platforms TikTok and Meta announced that they, too, are adding the same type of misinformation management framework for their sites.\n\nResearchers analyzed data relating to more than 40,000 X posts for which notes were proposed. They estimated that after a note was attached to a post, it resulted, on average, in 46.1% fewer reposts, 44.1% fewer likes, 21.9% fewer replies, and 13.5% fewer views.\n\nA recent study finds that \"crowdchecking\" (X's collaborative fact-checking experiment known as Community Notes) actually works. X posts with public correction notes were 32 percent more likely to be deleted by the authors than those with just private notes.\n\n### Effectiveness of Fact-Checking\n\nA Nature Human Behaviour paper from MIT Sloan reveals that fact-checker warning labels on social media can significantly reduce belief in and spread of misinformation, even among those who harbor doubts about the fact-checkers themselves.\n\nFact-checking primarily affects the specific fake news it directly addresses, whereas media literacy helps to distinguish between false and correct information more generally, both immediately and around two weeks after the intervention. Media literacy enables participants to critically evaluate social media postings, while fact-checking fails to enhance their skills as much.\n\n### Tools for Fact-Checking\n\nYou can use fact-checking websites like Snopes to see if a claim has been proven false. A very handy tool is to use a free AI chatbot to help fact-check suspicious information.\n\nHoaxy is a web-based tool that visualizes the spread of articles online. Hoaxy searches for claims and fact-checking going back to 2016. It tracks the sharing of links to stories from low-credibility sources and independent fact-checking organizations.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fc19be83-c5d4-4d22-a1ea-f9f460ee03af","uuid":"a68faf9d-4539-43b5-a314-e66e5a766e94","tool_use_result":{"query":"social media misinformation fact check 2026","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_018vPkRncYdak3tm38HzRSxA","content":[{"title":"COLUMN: How do you know if what you see on social media is real? - Marblehead Current","url":"https://marbleheadcurrent.org/2026/01/27/column-how-do-you-know-if-what-you-see-on-social-media-is-real/"},{"title":"Combating Misinformation by Sharing the Truth: a Study on the Spread of Fact-Checks on Social Media - PMC","url":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9188446/"},{"title":"You've been fact-checked! Examining the effectiveness of social media fact-checking against the spread of misinformation - ScienceDirect","url":"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S2772503023000506"},{"title":"Tools That Fight Disinformation Online | RAND","url":"https://www.rand.org/research/projects/truth-decay/fighting-disinformation/search.html"},{"title":"The most effective online fact-checkers? Your peers","url":"https://www.rochester.edu/newscenter/crowdsourcing-fact-checking-community-notes-social-media-676142/"},{"title":"Social Media Fact-Checking: The Effects of News Literacy and News Trust on the Intent to Verify Health-Related Information - PMC","url":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10606871/"},{"title":"Debunking Viral Claims Archives - FactCheck.org","url":"https://www.factcheck.org/fake-news/"},{"title":"Debunking “fake news” on social media: Immediate and short-term effects of fact-checking and media literacy interventions - ScienceDirect","url":"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S004727272500043X"},{"title":"Flagging misinformation on social media reduces engagement, study finds | Yale News","url":"https://news.yale.edu/2025/09/25/flagging-misinformation-social-media-reduces-engagement-study-finds"},{"title":"Warning labels from fact checkers work — even if you don’t trust them | MIT Sloan","url":"https://mitsloan.mit.edu/press/warning-labels-fact-checkers-work-even-if-you-dont-trust-them"}]},"Here are the search results for \"social media misinformation fact check 2026\":\n\n## Key Findings\n\n### Current State of Misinformation\nSocial media is filled with more false information than ever before. In recent months, experts have noticed a big rise in misinformation and disinformation online. Misinformation means sharing something wrong by mistake, while disinformation is a lie spread on purpose. Both are spreading quickly on platforms like Facebook, Instagram, X (formerly Twitter) and TikTok.\n\n### Recent Developments in Fact-Checking\n\nMeta (which owns Facebook and Instagram) recently decided to end its program of using outside fact-checkers on its platforms. Many people are worried that without those fact-checks, it might become even easier for fake posts to spread unchecked.\n\nFrom late 2016 to early 2025, FactCheck.org was one of several organizations working with Meta to debunk misinformation shared on Meta's social media platforms.\n\n### Community Notes and Crowdsourced Fact-Checking\n\nPointing out potentially misleading posts on social media significantly reduces the number of reposts, likes, replies, and views generated by such content. This suggests that crowd-sourced fact-checking can be a useful tool for curbing online misinformation.\n\nEarlier this year, the social media platforms TikTok and Meta announced that they, too, are adding the same type of misinformation management framework for their sites.\n\nResearchers analyzed data relating to more than 40,000 X posts for which notes were proposed. They estimated that after a note was attached to a post, it resulted, on average, in 46.1% fewer reposts, 44.1% fewer likes, 21.9% fewer replies, and 13.5% fewer views.\n\nA recent study finds that \"crowdchecking\" (X's collaborative fact-checking experiment known as Community Notes) actually works. X posts with public correction notes were 32 percent more likely to be deleted by the authors than those with just private notes.\n\n### Effectiveness of Fact-Checking\n\nA Nature Human Behaviour paper from MIT Sloan reveals that fact-checker warning labels on social media can significantly reduce belief in and spread of misinformation, even among those who harbor doubts about the fact-checkers themselves.\n\nFact-checking primarily affects the specific fake news it directly addresses, whereas media literacy helps to distinguish between false and correct information more generally, both immediately and around two weeks after the intervention. Media literacy enables participants to critically evaluate social media postings, while fact-checking fails to enhance their skills as much.\n\n### Tools for Fact-Checking\n\nYou can use fact-checking websites like Snopes to see if a claim has been proven false. A very handy tool is to use a free AI chatbot to help fact-check suspicious information.\n\nHoaxy is a web-based tool that visualizes the spread of articles online. Hoaxy searches for claims and fact-checking going back to 2016. It tracks the sharing of links to stories from low-credibility sources and independent fact-checking organizations."],"durationSeconds":19.0016011}}
[2026-02-04T00:03:39.359Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BhXXfAcryVS6eFVJBqmahL","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Elon Musk DOGE government spending cuts claims 2026\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Department of Government Efficiency - Wikipedia\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Department_of_Government_Efficiency\"},{\"title\":\"4 DOGE Proposed Cuts and the Impact On Your Wallet (and the Economy)\",\"url\":\"https://finance.yahoo.com/news/4-proposed-cuts-musk-doge-124507934.html\"},{\"title\":\"DOGE says it has saved $160 billion. Those cuts have cost taxpayers $135 billion, one analysis says. - CBS News\",\"url\":\"https://www.cbsnews.com/news/doge-cuts-cost-135-billion-analysis-elon-musk-department-of-government-efficiency/\"},{\"title\":\"DOGE Produced the Largest Peacetime Workforce Cut on Record, but Spending Kept Rising | Cato at Liberty Blog\",\"url\":\"https://www.cato.org/blog/doge-produced-largest-peacetime-workforce-cut-record-spending-kept-rising-0\"},{\"title\":\"Elon Musk's DOGE tally: The federal workforce is down while government spending is up\",\"url\":\"https://finance.yahoo.com/news/elon-musks-doge-tally-the-federal-workforce-is-down-while-government-spending-is-up-192850019.html\"},{\"title\":\"What has DOGE cut so far? | Fox Business\",\"url\":\"https://www.foxbusiness.com/politics/what-has-doge-cut-so-far\"},{\"title\":\"DOGE didn't save taxpayers $1 trillion, after all | On Point with Meghna Chakrabarti\",\"url\":\"https://www.wbur.org/onpoint/2026/01/20/doge-taxpayers-government-musk-agency\"},{\"title\":\"Elon Musk’s DOGE Gutted Federal Agencies, Cancelled Major Programs — But Federal Spending Still Went UP: Report\",\"url\":\"https://www.yahoo.com/news/articles/elon-musk-doge-gutted-federal-001321274.html\"},{\"title\":\"Musk’s DOGE Cuts Cripple Government Agencies—for a Fraction of Promised Savings\",\"url\":\"https://www.narfe.org/blog/2025/04/22/musks-doge-cuts-cripple-government-agencies-for-a-fraction-of-promised-savings/\"},{\"title\":\"What Musk's DOGE Really Cut: Trust, Safety, and Democracy - Roosevelt Institute\",\"url\":\"https://rooseveltinstitute.org/blog/what-musks-doge-really-cut-trust-safety-and-democracy/\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about Elon Musk's DOGE government spending cuts claims in 2026:\n\n## Initial Promises vs. Actual Results\n\nPresident Donald Trump appointed Elon Musk to lead the new Department of Government Efficiency (DOGE) to reduce government spending by up to $2 trillion by July 4, 2026. It was first suggested to Donald Trump by Elon Musk in 2024, and was officially established by an executive order on January 20, 2025.\n\n## Declining Savings Targets\n\nThe Department of Government Efficiency (DOGE) first set a goal to balance the budget by cutting $2 trillion in waste, fraud, and abuse. This goal was later reduced to $1 trillion and then again to just $150 billion.\n\nIn April of 2025, Musk announced that not only would DOGE lower its projected savings estimate for fiscal year 2026 from $1 trillion to $150 billion, but that his time allocation to DOGE would drop significantly to the extent of working one to two days per week with the department.\n\n## Disputed Claims and Fact-Checking\n\nIn April 2025, Musk stated that at that time $150 billion had been cut, but this figure was disputed by fact-checkers, and House DOGE caucus leader Blake Moore said on June 5 that Republican members always knew it was a \"massive exaggeration\".\n\nThe top 13 contracts claimed by DOGE \"were all incorrect,\" reported the Times, highlighting how the top two were for Defense Department contracts Musk claimed were \"terminations\" that had saved $7.9 billion. \"That was not true. The contracts are still alive and well, and those savings were an accounting mirage.\"\n\n## Spending Actually Increased\n\nIn fact, they didn't cut a dollar of federal spending. In the year that DOGE was active, when they were supposed to be saving $1 trillion, spending didn't go down at all. It went up.\n\nThe federal government spent $7.6 trillion in the first 11 months of calendar year 2025, approximately $248 billion higher by November of 2025 compared to the same month in 2024.\n\n## Workforce Impact\n\nDOGE did not reduce spending, but it did reduce federal employment by nine percent in less than 10 months. All told, federal rolls have fallen by more than 270,000 workers compared to when the year began.\n\n## Musk's Own Assessment\n\nElon Musk recently said that DOGE was only \"a little bit successful\" and that he wouldn't do it again.\n\nMusk and his inner circle left DOGE at the end of May. Trump stated that the entity's work will \"conclude\" no later than July 4, 2026.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fc19be83-c5d4-4d22-a1ea-f9f460ee03af","uuid":"37ea1ddf-a092-439a-802b-0d7261bb0388","tool_use_result":{"query":"Elon Musk DOGE government spending cuts claims 2026","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_012ghkEUgG4bodCGKAT3vHuz","content":[{"title":"Department of Government Efficiency - Wikipedia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Department_of_Government_Efficiency"},{"title":"4 DOGE Proposed Cuts and the Impact On Your Wallet (and the Economy)","url":"https://finance.yahoo.com/news/4-proposed-cuts-musk-doge-124507934.html"},{"title":"DOGE says it has saved $160 billion. Those cuts have cost taxpayers $135 billion, one analysis says. - CBS News","url":"https://www.cbsnews.com/news/doge-cuts-cost-135-billion-analysis-elon-musk-department-of-government-efficiency/"},{"title":"DOGE Produced the Largest Peacetime Workforce Cut on Record, but Spending Kept Rising | Cato at Liberty Blog","url":"https://www.cato.org/blog/doge-produced-largest-peacetime-workforce-cut-record-spending-kept-rising-0"},{"title":"Elon Musk's DOGE tally: The federal workforce is down while government spending is up","url":"https://finance.yahoo.com/news/elon-musks-doge-tally-the-federal-workforce-is-down-while-government-spending-is-up-192850019.html"},{"title":"What has DOGE cut so far? | Fox Business","url":"https://www.foxbusiness.com/politics/what-has-doge-cut-so-far"},{"title":"DOGE didn't save taxpayers $1 trillion, after all | On Point with Meghna Chakrabarti","url":"https://www.wbur.org/onpoint/2026/01/20/doge-taxpayers-government-musk-agency"},{"title":"Elon Musk’s DOGE Gutted Federal Agencies, Cancelled Major Programs — But Federal Spending Still Went UP: Report","url":"https://www.yahoo.com/news/articles/elon-musk-doge-gutted-federal-001321274.html"},{"title":"Musk’s DOGE Cuts Cripple Government Agencies—for a Fraction of Promised Savings","url":"https://www.narfe.org/blog/2025/04/22/musks-doge-cuts-cripple-government-agencies-for-a-fraction-of-promised-savings/"},{"title":"What Musk's DOGE Really Cut: Trust, Safety, and Democracy - Roosevelt Institute","url":"https://rooseveltinstitute.org/blog/what-musks-doge-really-cut-trust-safety-and-democracy/"}]},"Based on the search results, here's what I found about Elon Musk's DOGE government spending cuts claims in 2026:\n\n## Initial Promises vs. Actual Results\n\nPresident Donald Trump appointed Elon Musk to lead the new Department of Government Efficiency (DOGE) to reduce government spending by up to $2 trillion by July 4, 2026. It was first suggested to Donald Trump by Elon Musk in 2024, and was officially established by an executive order on January 20, 2025.\n\n## Declining Savings Targets\n\nThe Department of Government Efficiency (DOGE) first set a goal to balance the budget by cutting $2 trillion in waste, fraud, and abuse. This goal was later reduced to $1 trillion and then again to just $150 billion.\n\nIn April of 2025, Musk announced that not only would DOGE lower its projected savings estimate for fiscal year 2026 from $1 trillion to $150 billion, but that his time allocation to DOGE would drop significantly to the extent of working one to two days per week with the department.\n\n## Disputed Claims and Fact-Checking\n\nIn April 2025, Musk stated that at that time $150 billion had been cut, but this figure was disputed by fact-checkers, and House DOGE caucus leader Blake Moore said on June 5 that Republican members always knew it was a \"massive exaggeration\".\n\nThe top 13 contracts claimed by DOGE \"were all incorrect,\" reported the Times, highlighting how the top two were for Defense Department contracts Musk claimed were \"terminations\" that had saved $7.9 billion. \"That was not true. The contracts are still alive and well, and those savings were an accounting mirage.\"\n\n## Spending Actually Increased\n\nIn fact, they didn't cut a dollar of federal spending. In the year that DOGE was active, when they were supposed to be saving $1 trillion, spending didn't go down at all. It went up.\n\nThe federal government spent $7.6 trillion in the first 11 months of calendar year 2025, approximately $248 billion higher by November of 2025 compared to the same month in 2024.\n\n## Workforce Impact\n\nDOGE did not reduce spending, but it did reduce federal employment by nine percent in less than 10 months. All told, federal rolls have fallen by more than 270,000 workers compared to when the year began.\n\n## Musk's Own Assessment\n\nElon Musk recently said that DOGE was only \"a little bit successful\" and that he wouldn't do it again.\n\nMusk and his inner circle left DOGE at the end of May. Trump stated that the entity's work will \"conclude\" no later than July 4, 2026."],"durationSeconds":21.798455799999996}}
[2026-02-04T00:03:41.948Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Se9ZTU1NsySmLLFXHaw62N","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"pharmaceutical drug prices claims 2026\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Pharma Companies Raise List Prices, Including 16 That Had Agreements to Lower Prices with Trump Administration: Report | PharmExec\",\"url\":\"https://www.pharmexec.com/view/companies-raise-list-prices-16-agreements-lower-prices-trump-administration-report\"},{\"title\":\"Medicare Drug Price Negotiation Program: Negotiated Prices for Initial Price Applicability Year 2026 | CMS\",\"url\":\"https://www.cms.gov/newsroom/fact-sheets/medicare-drug-price-negotiation-program-negotiated-prices-initial-price-applicability-year-2026\"},{\"title\":\"Trump struck deals with 16 drug companies. But they're still raising prices this year\",\"url\":\"https://www.npr.org/2026/01/16/nx-s1-5678915/trumprx-pharma-drug-price-deals-list-prices\"},{\"title\":\"Drugmakers raise US prices on 350 medicines despite pressure from Trump | CNN\",\"url\":\"https://www.cnn.com/2026/01/01/health/drug-price-increases-2026\"},{\"title\":\"Major Changes to U.S. Government Pricing Requirements Finalized, With Some Wins for Pharma and Biotech | Insights | Sidley Austin LLP\",\"url\":\"https://www.sidley.com/en/insights/newsupdates/2025/10/major-changes-to-us-government-pricing-requirements-finalized-with-some-wins-for-pharma-and-biotech\"},{\"title\":\"Drug prices to rise despite Trump's new policies\",\"url\":\"https://thehill.com/policy/healthcare/5668053-us-drug-prices-rise-2026/\"},{\"title\":\"List of Medications and Vaccines Increasing in Price in 2026 - Newsweek\",\"url\":\"https://www.newsweek.com/medications-drugs-vaccines-price-increases-2026-11290128\"},{\"title\":\"Negotiated Prices Take Effect for Ten Drugs in 2026 - Medicare Rights Center\",\"url\":\"https://www.medicarerights.org/medicare-watch/2025/10/09/negotiated-prices-take-effect-for-ten-drugs-in-2026\"},{\"title\":\"Policy stacking and system logic: 2026 ushers in a new era of US drug pricing\",\"url\":\"https://www.simon-kucher.com/en/insights/policy-stacking-and-system-logic-2026-ushers-new-era-us-drug-pricing\"},{\"title\":\"U.S. Drug Pricing Year in Review: Reflections on 2025 and Getting Ready for 2026 | Insights | Sidley Austin LLP\",\"url\":\"https://www.sidley.com/en/insights/newsupdates/2025/12/us-drug-pricing-year-in-review-reflections-on-2025-and-getting-ready-for-2026\"}]\n\nHere's what I found regarding pharmaceutical drug prices and related claims for 2026:\n\n## Drug Price Increases in 2026\n\nPharmaceutical companies have raised list prices for 872 brand-name medications, with a median increase of 4% in 2026. The number of price increases for 2026 is up from the same point last year, when drugmakers unveiled plans for raises on more than 250 drugs.\n\n### Despite Trump Administration Deals\n\nDrug companies, including the 16 that made deals with the Trump administration, raised the prices of 872 brand-name drugs in the first two weeks of 2026, according to an analysis by 46brooklyn. All 16 drug companies that inked deals with the Trump administration over the past few months still raised some of their prices for 2026.\n\nThe pricing deals struck between the Trump administration and drugmakers apply to the Medicaid program, while most Americans are on commercial health plans. MFN pricing could have a negligible impact on Medicaid patients because the program already guarantees the lowest price offered to any commercial payer.\n\n## Medicare Drug Price Negotiation Program\n\nFor the first time, the law provides Medicare the ability to directly negotiate the prices of certain high expenditure, single source drugs without generic or biosimilar competition. The Centers for Medicare & Medicaid Services (CMS) selected ten drugs covered under Medicare Part D for the first cycle of negotiations for initial price applicability year 2026.\n\nThe first set of negotiated drug prices will go into effect in 2026 and are estimated to save $1.5 billion in annual out-of-pocket costs for Medicare beneficiaries while saving the Medicare program $6 billion per year.\n\nAfter the first round of negotiations in 2024, Medicare prices for 10 chosen drugs were reduced by 38% to 79%, with those discounts going into effect in January of 2026.\n\n## Specific Drug Price Changes\n\nPfizer announced the most increases, with hikes on about 80 drugs and vaccines. Most are below 10%, but Comirnaty, its COVID-19 vaccine, will rise by 15%.\n\nNot all changes are upward. Drugmakers will cut list prices on about nine medications, including a more than 40% reduction for Jardiance, a diabetes drug sold by Boehringer Ingelheim and Eli Lilly. Jardiance is among 10 drugs for which the U.S. government negotiated lower Medicare prices for 2026, forcing Boehringer and Lilly to slash its cost by two-thirds.\n\n## TrumpRx Direct-to-Consumer Platform\n\nThe Trump administration successfully enforced its \"most favored nation\" (MFN) policy on more than a dozen drugmakers this year, procuring agreements that ensure the companies will offer their products at MFN pricing. The direct-to-consumer platform called TrumpRx is expected to launch early in 2026.\n\n## Policy Outlook\n\n2026 kicks off a period when multiple effective dates converge, and policymakers are building the infrastructure to observe and enforce the interactions with more precision. Medicare negotiation, Inflation Reduction Act inflation-adjusted rebates, Part D redesign, 340B policy shifts, and new payment model tests are landing close enough together that they will start interacting in practice.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fc19be83-c5d4-4d22-a1ea-f9f460ee03af","uuid":"2fa0b087-c0c8-453e-93b7-ad28e0ffe1b4","tool_use_result":{"query":"pharmaceuti